4342 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Before designing\054 I\047d test these rather than treating them as established facts\072\n\nH1 \055 Time perception\072 Users perceive exercise as requiring more time than they can afford\056\nH2 \055 Minimum\055value problem\072 Users believe very short workouts aren\047t meaningful enough to bother doing\056\nH3 \055 Transition cost\072 Preparation and leaving the workstation create more friction than exercise itself\056\nH4 \055 Timing\072 Fitness apps remind users according to schedules rather than actual moments of availability\056\nH5 \055 Cognitive load\072 Choosing a workout becomes another decision during an already demanding day\056\nH6 \055 Social friction\072 Users may avoid desk exercises because they feel uncomfortable exercising around colleagues\056\nH7 \055 Motivation dependence\072 Traditional fitness products work better on high\055motivation days than stressful days\056\nH8 \055 Micro\055workout opportunity\072 Users may exercise more consistently if activity requires no equipment\054 no clothing change\054 no travel and only 1\0235 minutes\056)
     /K [ 68 ]
     /P 4343 0 R
     /Pg 4206 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

4343 0 obj
  << /K [ 4342 0 R ]
     /P 4354 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 4206 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

